{"h": {"measure": "P", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 125, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When node2->3 is absent, the direct 0->3 conv supplies a much larger share of the output's capacity, so adding it helps more."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A residual input->output shortcut mainly helps when deep conv paths exist; in skip/pool/empty cells it adds little."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 already removed, deleting edge 5 leaves only the 0->3 path, removing all intermediate computation."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the 0->3 edge, removing 2->3 removes a major or the only path to the output and loses the shortcut-less network's main capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none on 0->1 reactivates node 1 and its downstream edges, a bigger gain than swapping one existing op for another."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling a missing 0->2 edge adds a new path rather than just changing an op, giving a larger improvement."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When 0->2 is missing, node 2 depends solely on edge 2, so making it a strong conv matters much more."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If 1->2 is absent, edge 4 is node 1's only route to the output, so removing it effectively discards the 0->1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Re